WEBVTT

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:58.970
My mom has a key to that lock and do is to the rest of the world.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:05:59.920
How much?

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.560
Your time is there.

00:06:01.628 --> 00:06:03.628
that same family to us.

00:06:03.708 --> 00:06:04.708
Thank you.

00:07:56.684 --> 00:07:59.684
It's been 700 miles below the control unit.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:08.800
We are certain the force of this detonation will rupture the faults of the Earth's surface

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:14.760
and set up a chain reaction of explosion when the Earth's tension is broken.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.200
There are only 51 hours left. We better notify the President.

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:02.520
Uniform, alpha, double Zulu.

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:04.880
Unit niner, alpha 2.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:08.460
We have a slight hold at T minus 120.

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:11.010
This is a fuel pressure parity check.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:14.140
Repeat, hold at T minus 120.

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:26.810
It is T minus 120, so we'll have to make this very brief.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:28.880
You all know Colonel Price?

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:40.880
commander of our Project Astra. Colonel, why this trip to Venus? I understand it's over 160 million

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:46.250
miles away. It'll take you four months to get there, and you'll be gone for two years. Gentlemen,

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:52.360
we've come a long way in space flight in the last 10 years. Since 1965, our fixed satellites,

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:56.820
our space stations, our lunar landing, and base established there several years ago,

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:59.980
our probes of the outer solar system, all...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.670
All these efforts have helped prepare us for the payoff of phase one, putting man on Venus.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:09.450
Attention, countdown is resumed from T minus 120.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:14.160
Repeat, countdown is resumed from T minus 120.

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:16.570
Gentlemen, any more questions?

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:20.710
Yes, why the astronauts take the long way to get to a planet?

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:22.940
Instead of hopping straight across to it.

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:25.560
Will Dr. Haynes contact operator five?

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:28.900
Repeat, will Dr. Haynes contact operator five?

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:29.540
Urgent.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:38.610
Operator, get me ground control, then base security, and operator, keep this line open.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:46.040
Actually, we take the shortest route. I'll show you.

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:51.180
This is the inner solar system. Mars, Earth, Venus, and Mercury.

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:53.660
No, Venus is the next closest planet to the sun.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:59.360
Your question is, why don't we drop right down here to Venus, taking advantage of the sun's gravitation.

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:01.520
Venus wouldn't be there when we got there.

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:03.100
It travels along its own orbit.

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:04.500
You make a rendezvous with it?

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:05.350
Exactly.

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:07.970
Colonel, make this brief.

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:14.710
This is our starting point, and Venus at our point of rendezvous.

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:18.400
You get into orbit around the Earth as a launching point in space.

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:21.230
Then, taking advantage of the Earth's speed along its own orbit,

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:25.370
we take off into deep space on a ballistic course that ends here.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.480
Now we drop into a Venus orbit and prepare to land.

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:29.820
And it's as simple as that.

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:31.870
Nothing's that simple.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:33.760
How long will the journey take?

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:36.910
Barring unusual circumstances, four months to reach Venus.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:41.370
But counting the return trip and planned explorations, we'll be gone two years.

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:44.760
Well, what do you consider unusual circumstances?

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:47.040
Anything we're not prepared for.

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:49.860
Excessive radiation, meteors, unknown factors.

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:53.410
The time is T-minus 117 minutes.

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:58.280
All unauthorized personnel are instructed to clear the launch area.

00:11:58.850 --> 00:11:59.970
Second stage fueling...

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:09.780
will now begin light crew stand by repeat light crew stand by that includes me gentlemen well one

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:16.960
last question please yes what about your family your wives sweetheart that's the most difficult

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:22.690
part of the whole trip two years alone gentlemen two

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:37.540
Is that confirmed, Dr. Hanson?

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:38.740
Right from the top.

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:40.320
Mike, this is it.

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:41.060
Speed it up.

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:41.480
Right.

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:43.880
This is ground control operation.

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:44.650
Urgent.

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:47.300
Unauthorized personnel clear the area.

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:48.080
Repeat.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:51.020
Unauthorized personnel clear the area.

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:59.970
You still thinking all war horrors?

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:05.130
like me can't take it doesn't matter what i think doctor your technical knowledge gives you an

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:11.090
override on the computer data to the contrary i hope you make it frankly so do i anyhow it'll be

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:17.130
worth it you know i've dreamt of this adventure ever since i was a kid that's telling them doc

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:27.370
it's the only way to go i can think of other ways especially for you what's the matter i

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:29.970
navigator got the countdown jitters ten billion dollars

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.140
We're the taxpayers' money, and we've got to put up with clowns.

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:33.820
Oh, come on, you two. Cut it out.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:38.100
I just hope we're something more than guinea pigs for our brain trust out there.

00:13:38.910 --> 00:13:43.540
Attention. T-minus 98. Stage 1 fueling details. Stand by.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:48.700
Repeat. Stage 1 fueling details. Stand by.

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:52.900
Hey, Stage 1. That's the cold stuff. The locks.

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:54.150
What's happening?

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:56.430
We're speeding it up.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:59.980
That must be the weather. We're tied to those tracking cameras.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.850
Who cares about pictures?

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:06.600
Doctor, get those Pentagon penpushers off their lard and behind their computers.

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:09.260
Our lives depend on ballistics, not pictures.

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:12.080
Attention, all base security personnel.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:15.180
Attention, all base security personnel.

00:14:16.170 --> 00:14:17.630
This is a class one alert.

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:18.810
Condition red.

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:20.930
Alpha phase is in effect.

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:24.860
All civilians not actually engaged in the Astro countdown.

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:28.370
Report to security headquarters for reclassification.

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:29.530
Alert.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:31.050
They must be kidding.

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:33.070
Push-up went out with miniskirts.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:34.780
This is 1975.

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:36.940
Even if you kept up with your comic books,

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:38.640
you ought to know what China's been fooling around with.

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:43.680
Give me control.

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:47.990
All sacked personnel.

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:52.140
All leaves are canceled.

00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:55.070
Base now operating under martial law.

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:29.200
Checkouts are canceled. Set all timers from T-90 to T-50. Light pair to board at T-30.

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:32.030
Those checkouts can't be bypassed.

00:15:32.310 --> 00:15:33.450
It's a red alert, Mason.

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:35.040
The ICBMs are flying.

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:36.070
It's fairly simple.

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:37.690
This base is a strategic target.

00:15:37.810 --> 00:15:38.470
They want us airborne.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:39.660
What do you say, Doc?

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:40.860
Relax, Danny.

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:42.200
We'll know soon enough.

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:59.450
Sit up.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.960
off T-minus 30. Colonel, we can't let them bypass those checkouts. I've got to check with

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:13.020
security. Excuse me, gentlemen. We under attack? All I know, gentlemen, is that we're in some kind

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:17.470
of military crisis. May or may not be the big rumble, but you know the routine. All bases

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:22.790
scramble, and that includes our big bird out there. Colonel, what about those secondary checks?

00:16:23.610 --> 00:16:27.510
All right, get together. See if you can live with your pet fixes as they are. Let's go for anything

00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:29.970
short of a fuel leak. What's the use of launching a...

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:34.420
gonna blow it. You know as well as I do, without a full check out anything can happen. And we're

00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:37.840
gonna be out there two years. Anything can happen while we're standing here.

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:58.810
Yes, we have top priority for replacements on this flight.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:06.720
Colonel Donahue, orders from the president.

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:10.020
Gentlemen, what is the situation?

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:10.800
Red alert.

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:12.500
That is all we can say now.

00:17:13.190 --> 00:17:14.470
Russia has advised us that...

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:16.010
T minus 45 minutes.

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:17.840
Anyway, there's no time for that.

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:22.180
You are to replace three of your crew with three other officers.

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:22.860
Women?

00:17:23.530 --> 00:17:24.670
Now I've heard everything.

00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:26.400
Colonel, this is ridiculous.

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:28.340
It's absolutely insane.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:29.980
Gentlemen, I don't understand.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:59.370
understand. You will, Colonel, but there's no time to argue. What's this? Special sail cargo to go on board. Can't take extra weight, you know that. The weights have been calculated, Colonel. We three women weigh less than the men we're replacing. Oh, and just who do you have in mind replacing? They're in your orders, Colonel. Dr. Brown, flight surgeon. Me. Lieutenant Sharp, instrument tech and assistant navigator, Major Williams, co-pilot and systems engineer.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:00.520
Yes, sir.

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:02.740
Minus 44 minutes.

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:04.770
Pardon me, sir.

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:08.960
You or the Joint Chiefs or the President can order what you wish.

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.460
Personally, I think you're out of your minds.

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:14.100
Colonel Price, it's not in your province to judge.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:15.140
Isn't it?

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:15.500
No.

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:19.960
What about the emotional stability of a mixed crew in deep space for over two years?

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:22.320
Colonel, we're quite stable.

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:25.620
No special accommodations on that ship.

00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:27.240
There's no privacy at all.

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:29.980
Nor are we asking for any special...

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:31.190
Special privileges, sir.

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:37.480
Colonel, this is Dr. Marion Turner, flight surgeon, microbiologist.

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:43.100
Where do we put on our suit, sir?

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:44.480
There goes my stability.

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:46.370
What's the story, General?

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:47.450
What's going on?

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:48.490
General, let us in on it.

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:49.220
Let us in.

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:49.880
Take some shots.

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:50.920
Let us in.

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:54.600
Lieutenant Carlson, the computer has some attack meteorologist.

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:55.530
Aye.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:59.110
Major Bronski, co-pilot, revival specialist.

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:05.580
Russia? First woman on the moon. That is right. Fortunately, I was at the International Space

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:11.420
Conference in Washington when this emergency arose. I'm happy to say that my government has

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:17.090
authorized me to join you. Emergency? You haven't said anything yet, Doc. What can you say, Colonel?

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:22.280
It's a presidential order. There must be worse fates, Colonel. Gentlemen, I'd like to consult

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:28.320
our project director, Dr. Haynes. I'm sure he... You don't have time, Colonel. Get these women ready

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:29.970
at once. A minus one.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:35.740
Attention, Astro flight crew, stand by for van pickup at T-30.

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:37.260
Sorry, man.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:38.940
Three years of preparation.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:42.610
Well, at least my wife will appreciate these replacements.

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:44.170
Good luck, sir.

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:54.240
Ladies, I don't believe you.

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:57.020
I don't believe you.

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:59.960
You know, it'd be a practical side to...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.760
What do you mean like having your socks washed?

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:04.850
Everything okay?

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:06.400
A-okay.

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:19.370
Eight.

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:20.770
Stop it.

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:47.910
Control the Astro. Everything is a-okay from here. All systems are go and you have a good

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:58.100
climbing angle. Velocity is 3250 at T plus two minutes. Confirm time sync. Prepare for booster

00:20:58.100 --> 00:20:59.970
cutoff. Astro to...

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:03.800
B-E-C, A-OK, I'll go here.

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:13.680
Time sync, T-plus, 2 minutes, 15 seconds.

00:21:15.380 --> 00:21:17.010
Cut off, T-plus, 3.

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:18.640
Read you loud and clear.

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:21.630
Confirm B-E-C-O at T-plus, 3.

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:25.850
We don't like Dr. Perry's pulsing.

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:29.890
Have it made.

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:32.580
If you can only take the second stage into Earth orbit.

00:21:33.260 --> 00:21:35.640
Astra to GC, redo.

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:38.620
30 seconds to cut off.

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:41.490
Colonel Price, this is Dr. Turner.

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:42.940
Clear the air, Dr. Turner.

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:45.670
How much time do we have before second stage cut in?

00:21:46.190 --> 00:21:46.770
Clear the air!

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:49.980
Doctor, you will have several minutes at low G

00:21:49.980 --> 00:21:52.820
before the second booster takes us into Earth's orbit.

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:55.300
Ship's gravity control is on.

00:21:55.670 --> 00:21:56.390
Ground to Astra.

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:58.440
Dr. Turner has a point.

00:21:59.200 --> 00:21:59.980
Before second...

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:03.300
stage cut in. We are T plus 2 and 45 seconds.

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:33.070
Curt, sequence your checkouts. You've got two minutes before cut-in.

00:22:35.040 --> 00:22:36.700
Give me a half G on the gravity neutralizer.

00:22:37.560 --> 00:22:38.060
You got it.

00:22:38.920 --> 00:22:40.120
Colonel, what about Dr. Perry?

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:49.250
You'll have the chance.

00:22:59.080 --> 00:22:59.960
Dr. Perry must...

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:10.760
have pure oxygen. Now ask Aero Medical for his reading. Control to Astro. Flight attitude is

00:23:10.760 --> 00:23:18.460
fair. Roll sequence is programming in, changing azimuth to 75 degrees northeast. Do you read?

00:23:19.150 --> 00:23:28.680
Astro to GC, Roger. Take sequence 2-1 as follows.

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:37.350
Cabin temperature 90, air pressure 5.5, relative humidity 36 degrees.

00:23:39.070 --> 00:23:41.030
Sequence 2-5 next.

00:23:43.090 --> 00:23:43.710
Danny, read off.

00:23:45.420 --> 00:23:47.140
Telemetry and tracking of green here.

00:23:48.160 --> 00:23:49.360
Little hash from shielding.

00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:53.300
Colonel, I warned you not to bypass those subsystem checks.

00:23:53.730 --> 00:23:54.170
Take it, Colonel.

00:23:55.620 --> 00:23:56.980
Auto guidance is sluggish.

00:23:58.190 --> 00:23:59.470
Manual override seems...

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:07.700
okay pitch access is following computer control two degrees per second over ground control to

00:24:07.700 --> 00:24:14.760
aspirin dr turner the aeromed readings on dr perry dr turner you must let me run this ship

00:24:16.670 --> 00:24:24.420
pastor to ground come in one minute before firing second stage where is your fire commit data

00:24:32.490 --> 00:24:34.750
Repeat, where is your fire commit data?

00:24:37.200 --> 00:24:38.400
That's Perry's sequence.

00:24:39.290 --> 00:24:44.740
Major Bronski, get into your seat.

00:24:44.840 --> 00:24:45.880
We fire in less than a minute.

00:24:51.730 --> 00:24:52.530
Major Bronski!

00:24:56.700 --> 00:24:57.940
Capcom, two astros.

00:24:58.490 --> 00:24:59.970
Heat exchanges and pressure is...

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.680
status on sequencer units

00:25:02.680 --> 00:25:04.080
before program commit.

00:25:04.910 --> 00:25:06.050
Astro to Capcom.

00:25:06.960 --> 00:25:09.440
We are T plus 4 minutes and 10 seconds.

00:25:10.550 --> 00:25:12.690
What is your attitude for orbital entry?

00:25:13.550 --> 00:25:14.450
Are we hitting the slot?

00:25:15.380 --> 00:25:16.500
Capcom to Astro.

00:25:16.980 --> 00:25:18.020
Can't bring up your nose.

00:25:18.340 --> 00:25:20.260
Hit your overrides and fly by wire.

00:25:20.570 --> 00:25:22.490
We need 4 degrees vertical pitch.

00:25:23.750 --> 00:25:25.030
You are the automatic tanks on manual.

00:25:25.450 --> 00:25:25.970
Bring us up.

00:25:29.240 --> 00:25:29.840
I'm on wire.

00:25:38.540 --> 00:25:42.380
That's it, 15 seconds to second stage, cut in.

00:25:44.240 --> 00:25:47.370
Major Bronski, Danny, 15 seconds.

00:26:06.880 --> 00:26:29.050
sequencers on the gas generators. Committed. Everybody grab tight. Capcom to Astro. All lights green. 4, 2, 1, 0.

00:27:06.200 --> 00:27:07.680
Boy, Colonel, you're in the slot.

00:27:08.400 --> 00:27:09.540
Earth orbit established.

00:27:09.880 --> 00:27:13.260
Prepare for Venus launch at T plus 1100.

00:27:14.260 --> 00:27:15.620
Launch T plus 1100.

00:27:17.210 --> 00:27:17.790
Plus 11.

00:27:20.150 --> 00:27:21.030
Moving us ahead again.

00:27:22.300 --> 00:27:23.380
Ambustion sequence in.

00:27:23.750 --> 00:27:24.670
Purge valve screen.

00:27:25.380 --> 00:27:27.020
Gas generators full pressure.

00:27:27.680 --> 00:27:28.320
You're A-OK.

00:27:39.560 --> 00:27:51.650
You know, Dr. Perry might have lost his life if you hadn't.

00:27:52.370 --> 00:27:53.710
We're thinking of one life.

00:27:54.300 --> 00:27:55.640
The colonel was thinking of all of us.

00:27:56.400 --> 00:27:59.040
Escape velocity reducing to ballistic course speed.

00:28:00.090 --> 00:28:02.950
Dropping to 18,000 miles per hour.

00:28:04.560 --> 00:28:07.180
Cabin pressure up to 0.9 atmospheres.

00:28:09.000 --> 00:28:13.500
Set control to AGCS and secure a final flight mark.

00:28:16.410 --> 00:28:17.330
And here we are.

00:28:17.880 --> 00:28:19.400
The old girl didn't pop a rivet.

00:28:20.360 --> 00:28:23.240
Venus, open your arm.

00:28:24.090 --> 00:28:26.050
They sure pushed us out of Earth orbit fast.

00:28:28.400 --> 00:28:29.960
I got a feeling there's something more than a...

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:42.070
war involved. You'll have plenty of time to ask them. Everybody get unplugged. You know why we're

00:28:42.070 --> 00:28:49.600
here? No. Are you going to tell her? I hope she never has to find out.

00:29:20.920 --> 00:29:21.960
throwing out a good spectrum.

00:29:25.990 --> 00:29:26.750
